Simile Version 6.0 for Linux
============================

Before you start:
-----------------
Simile v6 is distributed as packages compatible with the RPM and DEB
package management systems. Be sure you have the right package for
your system. It should use the dependencies mechanism to pull in
everything else it requires, including the GNU c++ compiler.

To start the program:
---------------------
Type 'simile' to the command line.

On Debian-based systems, e.g., Ubuntu, you can link to the desktop
launcher /usr/share/simile-6.0/Run/Simile.desktop for an icon you can
click on to launch Simile.


License code:
-------------
When you run Simile for the first time, you will be prompted for your
name and organization, and also the license code you got from
Simulistics (unless it is an evaluation version). The name and
organization must match those you supplied to Simulistics when buying
Simile. Important: this information is case and whitespace sensitive!

Memory requirement:
-------------------
256MB available in main memory or swap space. Simile will attempt to run 
with less memory, but this will limit the size of model you can build.

Libraries:
----------
Simile requires the following GNU libraries to be installed:
libc.so.6 (GLIBC 2.13 or higher)
libm.so.6
libgcc_s.so.1
libdl.so.2

These are included in all distributions based on the gcc 4.x
compilers. Older distributions may not be up to date; either update
them or ask Simulistics to build copies of the executables for the
older libraries.

Happy Modelling
Simulistics Ltd
